<title>SWEDEN: Volvo Q1 car sales rise 18 pct.</title>
<headline>Volvo Q1 car sales rise 18 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo on Wednesday reported its sales and operating income by unit for the first three months of 1997 ending March 31 as follows:</p>
<p>  SALES (Mln SKR)			  Q1 97	Q1 96</p>
<p>  Volvo Cars				 23,068 vs 19,612</p>
<p>  Volvo Trucks			     10,937 vs 11,656</p>
<p>  Volvo Buses				 2,341 vs  1,895</p>
<p>  Volvo Construction Equipment	  3,688 vs  3,045</p>
<p>  Volvo Penta				 1,015 vs    964</p>
<p>  Volvo Aero				  1,507 vs    956</p>
<p>  Other and eliminations	   CHARGE 723 vs    827 CHARGE</p>
<p>  Automotive operations total	  41,833 vs 37,301</p>
<p>  Operations being divested		  16 vs  1,767</p>
<p>  VOLVO GROUP TOTAL			41,849 vs 39,068</p>
<p>  OPERATING INCOME (Mln SKR)	   Q1 1997    Q1 1996</p>
<p>  Volvo Cars				  1,068 vs    191 CHARGE</p>
<p>  Volvo Trucks				  304 vs    731</p>
<p>  Volvo Buses				    87 vs     69</p>
<p>  Volvo Construction			  309 vs    273</p>
<p>  Volvo Penta				    50 vs     17</p>
<p>  Volvo Aero				    119 vs     58</p>
<p>  Other and eliminations	    CHARGE 46 vs     13</p>
<p>  Automotive operations total	   1,891 vs    970</p>
<p>  Operations being divested	  CHARGE 3 vs    206</p>
<p>  VOLVO GROUP TOTAL			 1,888 vs  1,176</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
